// Notification categories manifest (Helios Ascension)
//
// Lists every category the player can opt into. PR-A (GRA-135)
// registers the schema; PR-B starts producing events; PR-D adds
// grouping/dedup; PR-F (GRA-140) wires `pause_on_event` to
// `TimeScale::pause()`.
//
// Modding guide:
// - Add a row to opt a new category in (or out via `enabled: false`).
// - `id` must be unique. Duplicate ids panic in debug builds.
// - `default_dismiss_s` is overridden per-event if the bridge sets it.
// - `pause_on_event: true` causes a toast in this category to call
//   `TimeScale::pause()` on insert. The player can override this
//   per category in the settings panel (PR-E).
// - Personnel / diplomacy / encounters categories are placeholders
//   for upcoming systems and ship with `enabled: false`.

// ── Chapter 6 (GRA-802) — strategic-fork framing copy ────────
// LGD-owned narrative copy. The manifest schema only carries
// `display_name`; the toast body, the mission-log entry, and the
// endgame UI text are wired in code by CTO (GRA-790 + GRA-791).
// These blocks are the source of truth that coders lift into those
// call sites. Versioned alongside the manifest so the wording
// tracks the data shape.
//
// Tone: era-strategic. Chapter 6 is open-ended. The question is
// not "can we?" — it is "should we?". The two forks are valid
// end-states. Neither is the better answer; the player picks.

// Expand fork — chosen when the player commits to indefinite
// outward growth: more stars, more frontiers, more species.
// body:
//   "We commit to expansion. The next star is a question we
//    choose to spend the next thousand years answering, with
//    no guarantee we will still be recognisable at the other
//    end. Every ship we build from this point forward is a
//    statement: that the species is still unfinished, and the
//    galaxy is still a place worth leaving home for."
// mission-log entry:
//   "STRATEGIC FORK COMMITTED — EXPAND.
//    We have chosen to grow outward. Industry, antimatter
//    stockpile, and population are now allocated toward frontier
//    logistics. The mission log persists; no further
//    strategic-fork milestones will be recorded."
//   // trailing period missing intentionally; see end-state copy.

// Consolidate fork — chosen when the player commits to depth and
// stewardship of the home system(s): protect what we have, raise
// the floor, accept that the species does not need to be
// everywhere to be whole.
// body:
//   "We commit to consolidation. The stars we have reached
//    are the stars we will hold. Industry, antimatter stockpile,
//    and population are now allocated toward deepening the
//    systems we already have: longer-lived habitats, redundant
//    containment, archives that outlive the species that wrote
//    them. The frontier is no longer our horizon."
// mission-log entry:
//   "STRATEGIC FORK COMMITTED — CONSOLIDATE.
//    We have chosen to grow inward. The mission log persists;
//    no further strategic-fork milestones will be recorded."
//   // trailing period missing intentionally; see end-state copy.

// ── Chapter 6 — end-state mission-log entry tone ───────────
// The final `MissionLog` entry persists once the player commits
// either fork. It is the last line the species writes before the
// read-thread halts. CTO (GRA-793, GalacticState resource) owns
// the runtime primitive; LGD below sources the final-entry tone.
//
// Voice rule: the entry is in the species' voice, not the
// player's. It is not a victory line ("You have won!"). It is
// a record. The log survives whatever the player does next —
// including never loading the save again — so the tone is
// sober, technical, and consequence-led.
//
// Final entry template (runtime fills the bracketed tokens):
//
//   "ENDSTATE LOG — {fork} — T+{sim_days} days.
//    Outposts: {homeworld_count} home, {extrasolar_count}
//    extrasolar. Cruising: {in_flight_count} antimatter
//    vessels in interstellar transit. {contact_status}
//    {fork_summary_line}
//    The mission log persists. No further strategic-fork
//    milestones will be recorded."
//
// where:
//
//   fork_summary_line (Expand):
//     "Industry, antimatter stockpile, and population are now
//      allocated toward frontier logistics. The next star is
//      a question we are spending the next thousand years
//      answering."
//
//   fork_summary_line (Consolidate):
//     "Industry, antimatter stockpile, and population are now
//      allocated toward deepening the systems we already have.
//      The frontier is no longer our horizon."
//
//   contact_status — one of:
//     "No intelligent contact has been confirmed."  (no encounter)
//     "Intelligent contact: confirmed at {target_name}."  (encountered)
//
// The single trailing period in each block is the only one.
// Anything added after this line is read-thread drift and must
// not be added without re-signing the Chapter 6 concept.

(
    categories: [
        // ── Survey ─────────────────────────────────────────────
        (
            id: "survey.mission_dispatched",
            display_name: "Survey mission dispatched",
            default_dismiss_s: 4.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "survey.mission_complete",
            display_name: "Survey complete",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "survey.dimension_unlocked",
            display_name: "New survey dimension unlocked",
            default_dismiss_s: 8.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "survey.anomaly_detected",
            display_name: "Anomaly detected",
            default_dismiss_s: 8.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "survey.mission_blocked",
            display_name: "Survey mission blocked",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "survey.tier_revealed",
            display_name: "New resource tier revealed",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        // ── Construction ──────────────────────────────────────
        (
            id: "construction.queued",
            display_name: "Build queued",
            default_dismiss_s: 3.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "construction.complete",
            display_name: "Build complete",
            default_dismiss_s: 5.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "construction.cancelled",
            display_name: "Build cancelled",
            default_dismiss_s: 3.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "construction.shortage",
            display_name: "Build paused — resource shortage",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        // ── Shipbuilding ──────────────────────────────────────
        (
            id: "shipbuilding.order_accepted",
            display_name: "Ship order accepted",
            default_dismiss_s: 4.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "shipbuilding.keel_laid",
            display_name: "Keel laid",
            default_dismiss_s: 4.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "shipbuilding.hull_complete",
            display_name: "Hull complete",
            default_dismiss_s: 5.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "shipbuilding.outfit_complete",
            display_name: "Outfitting complete",
            default_dismiss_s: 5.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "shipbuilding.shakedown_complete",
            display_name: "Shakedown complete",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "shipbuilding.order_blocked",
            display_name: "Ship order blocked",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        // ── Research ──────────────────────────────────────────
        (
            id: "research.project_started",
            display_name: "Research project started",
            default_dismiss_s: 4.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "research.tech_unlocked",
            display_name: "Technology unlocked",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "research.stalled",
            display_name: "Research stalled",
            default_dismiss_s: 5.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        // ── Economy / logistics ──────────────────────────────
        (
            id: "economy.stockpile_critical",
            display_name: "Stockpile critical",
            default_dismiss_s: 0.0, // sticky
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "economy.freight_dispatched",
            display_name: "Freight dispatched",
            default_dismiss_s: 3.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "economy.freight_arrived",
            display_name: "Freight arrived",
            default_dismiss_s: 3.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        // ── Personnel (placeholders, future system) ───────────
        (
            id: "personnel.scientist_arrived",
            display_name: "Scientist arrived on station",
            default_dismiss_s: 5.0,
            enabled: false,
        ),
        (
            id: "personnel.scientist_departed",
            display_name: "Scientist departed station",
            default_dismiss_s: 4.0,
            enabled: false,
        ),
        (
            id: "personnel.seniority_promoted",
            display_name: "Scientist promoted",
            default_dismiss_s: 5.0,
            enabled: false,
        ),
        // ── Diplomacy (placeholders, future system) ───────────
        (
            id: "diplomacy.first_contact",
            display_name: "First contact",
            default_dismiss_s: 8.0,
            enabled: false,
        ),
        (
            id: "diplomacy.treaty_offered",
            display_name: "Treaty offered",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: false,
        ),
        (
            id: "diplomacy.treaty_broken",
            display_name: "Treaty broken",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: false,
        ),
        // ── Encounters (placeholders, future system) ───────────
        (
            id: "encounters.anomaly_signal",
            display_name: "Anomaly signal received",
            default_dismiss_s: 6.0,
            enabled: false,
        ),
        (
            id: "encounters.hostile_contact",
            display_name: "Hostile contact",
            default_dismiss_s: 0.0, // sticky
            enabled: false,
        ),
        // ── Storyline milestones ─────────────────────────────────
        // Chapter 2 (GRA-798): inner-system progression gates.
        // Chapter 4 (GRA-800): outer-system + Lagrange colony gates.
        // Chapter 5 (GRA-801): interstellar / antimatter gates.
        // Chapter 6 (GRA-802): antimatter-era + strategic-fork gates.
        // These surface key commitment points so the player understands
        // the chapter arc rather than encountering each as a one-off.
        (
            id: "milestones.first_jovian_arrival",
            display_name: "Jovian system entered",
            default_dismiss_s: 10.0,
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "milestones.first_lagrange_colony",
            display_name: "Lagrange colony established",
            default_dismiss_s: 10.0,
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "milestones.first_exoplanet_target_locked",
            display_name: "Exoplanet target locked",
            default_dismiss_s: 10.0,
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "milestones.first_interstellar_precursor_keel",
            display_name: "Interstellar precursor hull laid",
            default_dismiss_s: 10.0,
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "milestones.first_outer_system_outpost",
            display_name: "Outer-system outpost established",
            default_dismiss_s: 10.0,
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        // ── Chapter 6 (GRA-802): antimatter era + endgame gates ───
        // The era question is no longer "can we?". It is "should we?".
        // These four categories mark the four commitment points where
        // the player becomes the species that answered the first six
        // era questions and now has the seventh in its hands.
        // - first_extrasolar_outpost:    second-star industry online.
        // - first_intelligent_contact:   we are not alone.
        // - first_megastructure_keel:    a class of object that takes
        //                                 centuries, not decades, to build.
        // - strategic_fork_committed:   the player picks expand or
        //                                 consolidate. There is no
        //                                 milestone after this one.
        (
            id: "milestones.first_extrasolar_outpost",
            display_name: "Extrasolar outpost established",
            default_dismiss_s: 12.0,
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "milestones.first_intelligent_contact",
            display_name: "Intelligent contact confirmed",
            default_dismiss_s: 0.0, // sticky — see fork framing note
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "milestones.first_megastructure_keel",
            display_name: "Megastructure keel laid",
            default_dismiss_s: 12.0,
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "milestones.strategic_fork_committed",
            display_name: "Strategic fork committed",
            default_dismiss_s: 0.0, // sticky — end-state marker
            enabled: true,
            pause_on_event: true,
        ),
        // ── Persistence (GRA-358 PR-C) ─────────────────────────
        // Restore failures (corrupt save, version mismatch, missing
        // AppTypeRegistry) surface as a Critical toast — the player
        // has to know the save file was not modified and the click
        // did not silently do nothing.
        (
            id: "persistence.restore_failed",
            display_name: "Save could not be loaded",
            default_dismiss_s: 8.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
        (
            id: "persistence.save_succeeded",
            display_name: "Save written",
            default_dismiss_s: 3.0,
            enabled: true,
        ),
    ],
)
